error[AttributeError]: Loop `while fast is not None and fast.next is not None:`, so that `fast.next.next` is only read when `fast.next` is a node.
hint: Use `slow` and `fast`, both starting at the head.
hint: While `fast` and `fast.next` are nodes, move `slow` one node and `fast` two.
hint: Return `slow.val`.
right: `fast` covers the list twice as fast, so when it reaches the end, `slow` is halfway: O(n), in one pass.
wrong: Move `slow` one node and `fast` two nodes at a time, while `fast is not None and fast.next is not None`, then return `slow.val`. Counting the nodes and walking n // 2 links works too.

